> I think this might be a bit of a myth.  Adult dragons have a base
> difficulty of 20, once your character is quest elligible, the average
> of your level and a dragons difficulty is 17 (or higher).

You can track the way monster difficulty vs. level works very
accurately in extinctionist games: a monster will indeed only get
generated normally if (your level + dungeon level)/2 is at least as
high as the monster's difficulty. Before that, create monster spells
and stochastic level restocking will _not_ generate it.

There are of course the exceptions of polymorph, growing up, chameleon
shapechange, reverse genocide and possibly summon nasty spells.
And dragons can be generated several levels "out of depth" in throne
rooms.

> Arch liches and master liches are covetous. 

Which means they will pick up the game artefacts and your quest
artefact when those are sitting on the ground, and they will also
hover close to them (i.e. accurately teleport to whoever is carrying
them) unless scared. In order to take them from you, they'd need to
have a "steal amulet" melee attack.

